From 03c3c5466bf1bda7184d3fec4d525ec7c0586043 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "F. Duncanh" <fduncanh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:10:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 15/29] reworked the reverse-HTTP (EVENT) parsing

PTTH connections renamed EVENT connections.
EVENT/1.0 is an Apple one-way protocol that
sends messages from the client that can be
(optionally) acted on by the server, but
need no response.  Both reverse HTTP responses
and EVENT messages are now correctly parsed.

(cherry picked from commit 3fda79005f7be2da2faff36d206b9a509aa11e00)
